{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The reason this sacrifices section is joined [to the preceding parashah] is that HaShem then commanded Moses to command the children of Israel concerning the sacrifices they are obligated to perform, for he will not enter the land with them. And he began by mentioning the עלת תמיד [daily burnt offering]. Now if it is mentioned first, it is possible that the one mentioned is the one [given] at Mount Sinai, or else the arrangement of the sacrifices is ordered."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:42.068687340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}